  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LuciferCore High-Throughput HTTP Milestone (188k+ RPS)\n\n      - This release pushes throughput to a stable 188k+ requests per second and drops latency to under 480 microseconds by removing heavy internal dictionary caches and shifting to hardware-friendly flat structures.\n      - The internal Utf8Map header lookup cache has been stripped. Headers and cookies are now stored in tightly packed linear arrays managed via custom HeaderEntry struct wrappers, completely replacing generic ValueTuple wrappers and hashing overhead. This shifts lookups to high-speed linear scans (O(k)) that execute directly on CPU registers using SIMD vectorization.\n      - Dead-code fields, including the internal _cacheSize tracking variable, have been removed from the parser loops to eliminate redundant memory writes. These changes ensure optimal L1/L2 hardware prefetching and unshakeable throughput stability under extreme load.",
